# Written by coder B, 2026-11-26. NOT directly appliable to victory-fox: the hunks below are
# victory-dev's own (`git -C victory-dev diff HEAD`), verbatim, as the exact reference.
# The translator side is in par/foxB branch portB (commit "Picture fixes of ours on cool_fox").
#
# Contract (translator -> host), as in victory-dev:
#  - victory_shader::emit::HostShader gains `pub half_views: Vec<(u8, u32)>`: (root parameter
#    slot of a RootType::Table, dword offset of the descriptor in that table). The shader
#    reads/writes these views through an UNSIGNED-INTEGER typed handle (bufferLoad.i32 /
#    bufferStore.i32, component type 0x405).
#  - The host must show the shader, at those table places, a 16-bit FLOAT or SINT buffer view
#    as the UINT format of the same layout (R16_FLOAT/SINT -> R16_UINT, R16G16_* -> R16G16_UINT,
#    R16G16B16A16_* -> R16G16B16A16_UINT): `descriptor::host::half_view` below, used where the
#    draw/dispatch copies table views to host slots (victory-dev draw.rs hunks @@ -2520 and
#    @@ -2635: before `host.make_at(index, &view)` for a table place listed in half_views,
#    use `half_view(&view).unwrap_or(view)`), and the pipeline key must include half_views
#    (draw.rs @@ -1009: `h.extend_from_slice(&t.host.half_views)`), plus the one-line log
#    `note_half_views` (draw.rs @@ -3186) and the meter line in host.rs.
#  - UINT views at those places need nothing (run 92: the game's views there were already
#    UINT: "the host made 0 unsigned twins"); the twin matters for FLOAT/SINT views only.
#    Without this host part a FLOAT view at a halves place is read through a uint handle
#    (format/type mismatch, undefined): if C cannot land it, run with VICTORY_HALF_VIEWS=0
#    and cool_fox's view kinds (SLOT_TABLE_STRIDES=252) take those accesses.
#  - Shader cache entry format (crates/victory-gpu/src/shader_cache.rs, B's file) already
#    carries half_views in portB; cache key bumped ("victory shader cache key foxB 1").
#  - cool_fox's own host half of view kinds (write_stride, SLOT_TABLE_STRIDES=252,
#    view_stride_and_kind) stays as it is; nothing in portB changes slot numbers.
#  - New translator exports C may log once a run: victory_shader::emit::{HALVES_PLACES,
#    D16_VIEW_KIND_ACCESSES, D16_BITS_ACCESSES, WAVE_PAIRED_BEFORE_WIDE} (AtomicU64 counters),
#    and victory_shader::emit::d16_view_kinds() (VICTORY_D16_VIEW_KINDS, default on) if the
#    host wants to skip writing kind bits when it is off.
#  - Mesh linking (26600c6, emit::link_mesh / mesh_fits) is now in the translator; its host
#    half (pipeline/host.rs, VICTORY_MESH_LINK) is soldsawn 26600c6's pipeline/host.rs hunk:
#    `git -C C:/GTAVI/Tools/victory-dev show 26600c6 -- crates/victory-gpu/src/pipeline/host.rs` (C's call).
